t would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"63.83516483516483\" cy=\"370.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 6%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"77.75217391304348\" cy=\"360.8985507246377\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"98.58048780487803\" cy=\"306.5365853658537\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 24%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"141.44285714285712\" cy=\"216.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 42%&amp;#10;It rained 57% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"208.14319999999998\" cy=\"173.30666666666664\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 68%&amp;#10;It rained 60% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"297.0227397260274\" cy=\"162.6027397260274\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 70% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"400.5059259259259\" cy=\"125.85185185185185\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(27%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Houston the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.45) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.01).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>-0.012</td><td class='num'>13.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'>0.308</td><td class='num'>9.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>0.360</td><td class='num'>1.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'>0.446</td><td class='num'>4.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":29.76328,"lon":-95.36327,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Houston","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":213,"obs":0.014084507042253521,"sig":true},{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.016483516483516484,"n":91,"obs":0.03296703296703297,"sig":false},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.055797101449275355,"n":69,"obs":0.057971014492753624,"sig":false},{"hi":0.18,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.11463414634146339,"n":82,"obs":0.2073170731707317,"sig":true},{"hi":0.32,"lo":0.18,"mean":0.2357142857142857,"n":77,"obs":0.45454545454545453,"sig":true},{"hi"